  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "**do** (main verb) covers many actions that other languages name with separate verbs: *do the dishes* (wash), *do your hair* (brush or style), *do a degree* (study). Translate by the action meant, not word for word.",
    "grammar": "**do** (main verb) takes the helping **do** in questions and negatives like any ordinary verb, so the word can appear twice: *What do you do?*, *I didn't do it.* Learners often drop one of the two.",
    "culture": null,
